.TH SHEAF 1 "November 2026" "sheaf 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sheaf \- library of recent and favorite files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sheaf
[\fB\-\-quick\fR]
.br
.B sheaf
\fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sheaf shows the files you recently opened and the ones you marked as favorites. With no command it starts the window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-quick
Show only the quick open popup.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list, search \fR[\fIquery\fR]
List files that match the query.
.TP
.B open \fIpath\fR
Open a file.
.TP
.B favorite add|remove|list
Manage favorites.
.TP
.B tag add|remove|list
Manage tags.
.TP
.B forget \fIpath\fR
Remove a file from the library.
.TP
.B clear\-recent \-\-yes
Clear the recent files list.
.TP
.B clean \fR[\-\-dry\-run]
Forget files that no longer exist.
.TP
.B groups
List the groups.
.TP
.B paths
Show where Sheaf keeps its files.
.TP
.B import\-thingy
Import favorites and groups from Thingy.
.TP
.B export, import
Write or read the library as a JSON file.
.SH SEARCH
Free words, "quoted phrases", \-excluded words, tag:name, type:pdf, in:folder, is:fav and is:missing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sheaf/library.db
Favorites, tags and history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sheaf/
Settings and groups.
